Q: to attach an event to each element of an array
A: <p><code>icon_set</code> is a raw JavaScript <code>Array</code>. It doesn't have an <code>each</code> method. Use <code>Array.prototype.forEach</code> or <code>$.each</code> and wrap each array element with <code>$();</code></p>

<pre><code>icon_set.forEach(function (el) {
    $(el).mouseleave(function () {
        $(this).stop().fadeOut();
    });
});
</code></pre>

<p>or</p>

<pre><code>$.each(icon_set, function(index, el) {
  $(el).mouseleave(function () {
    $(this).stop().fadeOut();
  });
});
</code></pre>

<p>And prefer using the array literal syntax(<code>[]</code>) over the <code>Array</code> constructor</p>

